{
  "id": "28986_kantaku",
  "headword": "{干拓|かんたく}",
  "reading": "かんたく",
  "romaji": "kantaku",
  "part_of_speech": "noun, suru verb",
  "gloss": "land reclamation (by draining)",
  "definitions": [
    {
      "sense_number": 1,
      "gloss": "land reclamation (by draining wetlands or tidal flats)",
      "explanation": "Reclaiming usable land from a wetland, lake, or tidal flat by enclosing it with dikes and draining the water. Distinct from filling water in with soil, which is called {埋|う}め{立|た}て."
    }
  ],
  "examples": [
    {
      "id": "28986_kantaku_ex1",
      "japanese": "{広大|こうだい}な{干潟|ひがた}が{干拓|かんたく}された。",
      "english": "A vast tidal flat was reclaimed.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "28986_kantaku_ex2",
      "japanese": "この{農地|のうち}は{江戸時代|えどじだい}に{干拓|かんたく}されたものだ。",
      "english": "This farmland was reclaimed back in the Edo period.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "28986_kantaku_ex3",
      "japanese": "{干拓|かんたく}{事業|じぎょう}は{環境|かんきょう}への{影響|えいきょう}が{大|おお}きいと{批判|ひはん}されている。",
      "english": "Land reclamation projects are criticized for their large environmental impact.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    }
  ],
  "notes": "Composed of {干|ほ}す (to dry) + {拓|ひら}く (to open up land). The verb form is {干拓|かんたく}する.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {干拓|かんたく}する: to reclaim land by draining\n- {干拓|かんたく}{事業|じぎょう}: land reclamation project\n- {干拓地|かんたくち}: reclaimed land\n- {干潟|ひがた}を{干拓|かんたく}する: to reclaim a tidal flat\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {埋|う}め{立|た}て: landfill — fills water with earth or waste to create land, rather than draining\n- {開拓|かいたく}: pioneering; cultivating new land — broader, often about opening up forest or wilderness for farming",
